BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:141ca5e040eb6fab@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260917T165638Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] State of Maine v. Heather Marichal
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT Reporter of Decisions \nDecision:
   2026 ME 100 \nDocket: And-25-7 \nArgued: September 11\, 2025 \nDecided: 
  September 17\, 2026 \n \nPanel:  STANFILL\, C.J.\, and MEAD\, CONNORS\, L
 AWRENCE\, and DOUGLAS\, JJ.  \n \n \nSTATE OF MAINE \n \nv. \n \nHEATHER M
 ARICHAL \n \n \nSTANFILL\, C.J. \n[¶1]  Heather Marichal appeals from a j
 udgment of conviction for \ncriminal OUI (Class D)\, 29-A M.R.S. § 2411(1
 -A)(A) (2026)\, entered by the trial \ncourt (Androscoggin County\, Archer
 \, J.) following her conditional guilty plea.  \nThe issue before us is wh
 ether the court abused its discretion or violated \nMarichal’s constitut
 ional rights by denying Marichal’s motion to continue after \na defense 
 witness did not appear on the date of trial.  We affirm. \nI.  BACKGROUND 
 \n[¶2]  “The following facts are drawn from the State’s summary of th
 e \nevidence that it would have presented to a fact finder if [Marichal] h
 ad not \npleaded guilty.”  State v. Murray-Burns\, 2023 ME 21\, ¶ 2\, 2
 90 A.3d 542.  On or \nabout October 1\, 2021\, Marichal was driving down C
 ourt Street in Auburn.  She \n \n \n2 \ndrove onto the wrong side of the r
 oad and crashed into another vehicle.  Her \nvehicle then ricocheted off t
 hat vehicle and veered off the road onto a \nneighboring property\, striki
 ng a snowplow in the driveway.  Marichal told a \nresponding police office
 r that she had been at a “brew fest” and had consumed \nalcohol.  Mari
 chal also told the officer that she was the driver and sole occupant \nof 
 the vehicle.  Marichal took an Intoxilyzer test\, which indicated that her
  \nblood-alcohol content was .21 grams of alcohol per 210 liters of breath
 . \n[¶3]  In October 2021\, the State charged Marichal by complaint with 
 \ncriminal OUI\, 29-A M.R.S. § 2411(1-A)(A).  The trial was continued sev
 eral times \nin 2022 and 2023 for reasons that are not clear from the reco
 rd.  The case was \nincluded on the trial list as a backup for September 2
 023\, December 2023\, and \nFebruary 2024.  Each time\, the case was not r
 eached for trial. \n[¶4]  On\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/law
 court/2026/26me100.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me100.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:55e856d4e7efe0f3@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260915T211950Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: Knox County Probate Court
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
